From: Chinmoy Dey <chinmoy@nexthop.ai>
Date: Fri, 02 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Switch-Host power events and supported ResetTypes

Wire the rmc-events host state monitor into bmcweb and restrict
ComputerSystem.Reset to the ResetTypes backed by a rack-manager command:
  - meson.build: add host_state_monitor.cpp to sources
  - event_service_manager.hpp: include and instantiate the
    DbusHostStateMonitor (CurrentHostState PropertiesChanged on
    xyz.openbmc_project.State.Host host0 -> ResourceEvent
    ResourcePoweredOn/Off, ResourcePoweringOn/Off with OriginOfCondition
    /redfish/v1/Systems/system)
  - event_service.hpp: add "ResourceEvent" registry prefix and
    "ComputerSystem" resource type to the supported subscription filters
  - systems.hpp: accept only On, ForceOff, GracefulShutdown and PowerCycle;
    every other ResetType (ForceOn, ForceRestart, GracefulRestart, Nmi, ...)
    returns ActionParameterNotSupported instead of being silently mapped
    to a transition the Switch-Host cannot perform
  - systems.hpp: ResetActionInfo advertises the same four values. The
    stock code always adds Nmi and expands AllowedHostTransitions.On into
    On and ForceOn, so clients were offered ResetTypes the POST path
    rejects. Nmi and ForceOn are no longer advertised and the
    property-not-implemented fallback lists only On and GracefulShutdown
  - systems.hpp: getStopBootOnFault meant to ignore a missing
    xyz.openbmc_project.Settings service (EBADR / EHOSTUNREACH) but the
    condition was written with || so it is always true and every error
    became 500 InternalError. SONiC has no Settings daemon, so GET
    /redfish/v1/Systems/system always failed. Use && as the comment intends
  - systems.hpp: afterPortRequest treats the systemd ListUnits / socket
    Listen lookups behind SerialConsole as an optional provider. SONiC has
    no systemd on the system bus, so the lookup fails with EIO and used to
    turn an otherwise complete GET /redfish/v1/Systems/system into 500
    InternalError. SerialConsole is now omitted instead
  - dbus_utils.cpp: when the D-Bus service owning the property is not on
    the bus (EHOSTUNREACH, i.e. sonic-dbus-bridge down), afterSetProperty
    returns 503 ServiceTemporarilyUnavailable with Retry-After instead of
    404 ResourceNotFound, so a POST ComputerSystem.Reset while the bridge
    is restarting is reported as retryable

The monitor implementation lives in rmc-events/ and is copied into the
bmcweb tree by the build system before this patch is applied.
---
